d\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a396bd1202bc4e812c7ab9796c82f5c85b129a73e1f07cd244324f81be3b4af1","event_uuid":"24d352fd-1d94-479e-b6c9-4c1385207587","position":{"commit_sha":"59acc6c8fdfa9b88e002bcb852bfa9e3e18cdfdf","position":"1787029990569454001-24d352fd-1d94-479e-b6c9-4c1385207587"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4629f60a4e683a083f0d2c140a50afb7ce808bb2bf8d44395b6a97d4a0dc90e3","event_uuid":"6ad4950e-32ff-427d-a29c-5f8c2dbaffd2","position":{"commit_sha":"32498bdf7b5bb4a9194139a31e6f79c18d6a0e04","position":"1787030157100461001-6ad4950e-32ff-427d-a29c-5f8c2dbaffd2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6df5607be0d2c7fbe89e569fb34bd650f8a796e7f9a9ceaec9fa92f55e0ada67","event_uuid":"49781188-8b83-4d3f-9649-33d7f29b4143","position":{"commit_sha":"32498bdf7b5bb4a9194139a31e6f79c18d6a0e04","position":"1787030158075198001-49781188-8b83-4d3f-9649-33d7f29b4143"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786995183192552001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bdd3daad-3a5e-4c57-a208-04876d60fb2c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe op-cert service does per-job boto3/SSM/region lookup and patches process-global key/principal/push state — coupling app config to one secret store, letting jobs observe different keys, and creating concurrency/cleanup hazards. ADR 0098 keeps SSM as a deployment storage option but moves application binding to startup.\n## Outcome\nAt startup accept exactly one of preferred `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` or compat `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`. Validate before queue/worker/network/workspace creation, copy into a process-owned 0700 dir/0600 file, build one immutable signer/runtime, and pass signer/principal/push policy context-locally to jobs. The process never rereads; restart observes replacement.\n## Plan\n1. Replace `opcert_service.ssm`/per-job key acquisition with startup composition in config/key-provider/app. Reject missing, both-set, unreadable, non-regular, malformed, encrypted/passphrase, or non-Ed25519 input before service work. The path source (`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`) also needs a 0600-or-stricter regular-file check. Both are copied to the process-owned 0700/0600 location, mode-checked after copy.\n2. Copy key bytes to a process-owned runtime dir/file at 0700/0600; never modify/delete the deployment source. Graceful shutdown removes only Rebar's copy; deployment tmpfs/restart owns crash cleanup.\n3. Replace global environment/state patching with a typed context-local signer, principal, and push policy threaded through jobs/workspace/signing. Concurrent/timed-out workers cannot observe or mutate one another's context.\n4. **Thread the immutable signer through the out-of-`opcert_service/` producer seams (BOTH job kinds).** Key/principal are read from `os.environ` in `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py` (`ensure_opcert_key`→`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` ~L169; `opcert_principal`→`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` ~L193; both called by `mint_opcert_record`). Both producer chains converge on `signing._sign_manifest_under_lock` (`signing.py:528`, calling `mint_opcert_record` at L567): (a) COMPLETION — `transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict`→`signing.sign_manifest` (`:587`); (b) PLAN-REVIEW — `attest.py:202`→`generation.sign_manifest` (`generation.py:261`, calling `_sign_manifest_under_lock` at `:334`). Convert `_sign_manifest_under_lock`, both `sign_manifest` entrypoints, and `sign_completion_verdict` to accept+forward an optional `OpcertSigner` binding (signer-key-handle + principal); the service supplies its startup-bound context-local signer to BOTH job dispatches, so removing `keyprov.py`'s `os.environ` patching (today binding the key for both kinds) cannot silently break either path. Developer-local close/review-plan callers pass no binding, keeping the env/genesis default. Also route the push-policy site (`_push_mode`/`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH`) to the context-local policy when bound, env default otherwise.\n5. Decouple the op-cert APPLICATION runtime from SSM/region: remove `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM` and the key-retrieval `AWS_REGION`/`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` from the opcert service env in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, drop the app runtime boto3 need in `infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert`, and materialize the key OUTSIDE the app before start (`infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh`). HOSTED KEY MATERIALIZATION (T10): the multiline Ed25519 PEM cannot live in a single-line `.env`, so mirror the `rebar-bot-signing-key` precedent (`fetch-secrets.sh:93-115`) — `fetch-secrets.sh` writes the SSM value to a 0600 FILE next to `.env` (ALWAYS created, empty when the slot is blank, per bug beb1, so the bind-mount source is never an auto-created directory) and exports only its PATH; the opcert compose service bind-mounts that file `:ro` at a fixed container target (like docker-compose.yml:234) and sets `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` to it. The file-path source is authoritative for the hosted deployment; inline `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY` is NOT used there. The shared `/rebar/prod/*` SSM grant `ssm_params_read` in `iam.tf` (co-used by origin-guard/gerrit, no opcert app-role) is NOT dropped — decoupling is only at the app-runtime boundary.\n6. Preserve ADR 0049's Ed25519/DSSE algorithm, trust roots/eras, producer, authoritative fetch, envelope persistence, guard, and no-workspace-push invariants.\n\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Startup component tests instrument queue, worker, network, and workspace factories and assert every invalid source fails before all four.\n- Filesystem tests assert source untouched, process dir 0700, copy 0600, stable bytes after source replacement, restart observes new bytes, cleanup removes only the copy, and stale tmpfs clears on container restart.\n- **Signer-seam tests** assert BOTH producer chains (completion `sign_completion_verdict`→`signing.sign_manifest`, plan-review `generation.sign_manifest`, both via `_sign_manifest_under_lock`→`mint_opcert_record`/`ensure_opcert_key`/`opcert_principal`) sign from the passed context-local binding (not `os.environ`) when the service supplies one — proven with a distinct injected key while `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`/`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` are unset — and with no binding resolve via env/genesis (regression pin).\n- Concurrent/timed-out job tests use distinct principals/policies and prove context isolation, immutable startup signer, and no workspace push remote.\n- Structural tests assert `src/rebar/opcert_service` has no boto3/SSM/region import or runtime parameter after cutover, the opcert compose env carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region, the image needs no runtime boto3, and `fetch-secrets.sh` materializes the opcert key to a 0600 file bind-mounted `:ro` with `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` (shared iam.tf SSM grant untouched).\n- [operator-attested] Hosted signing canary records deployment/run ids, source kind (never value), signature verification, restart result, modes, and redacted failure outcome.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nExpand deployment input first while the legacy per-job facade exists; pre-removal rollback selects the legacy facade, post-removal rollback needs the same startup source contract (signatures/envelopes stay compatible).\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly-one source validation rejects every named invalid case before queue, worker, network, or workspace construction.\n- [ ] The process-owned copy is 0700/0600, stable for process lifetime, observes replacement only after restart, and cleanup never alters the deployment source.\n- [ ] Concurrent and timed-out jobs prove context-local signer/principal/push isolation, one immutable startup signer, existing signature verification, and no workspace push remote.\n- [ ] Both out-of-`opcert_service/` signing producer chains — completion (`_opcert_signing.py`, `signing.sign_manifest`+`_sign_manifest_under_lock`, `transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict`) and plan-review (`generation.py:sign_manifest`, `attest.py`) — sign from the injected context-local binding when the service supplies one (to BOTH job kinds), and the developer-local close/review-plan paths retain prior env/genesis resolution unchanged (regression pinned).\n- [ ] The op-cert application runtime (`src/rebar/opcert_service` process/container) has no SSM/boto3/region/key-parameter dependency: the compose service carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region, the image needs no runtime boto3, and the key is materialized before start by `fetch-secrets.sh` to a 0600 file bind-mounted `:ro` with `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`. The shared `/rebar/prod/*` instance-role SSM grant in `iam.tf` is deliberately UNCHANGED (co-used by origin-guard/gerrit, not an app-role).\n- [ ] Secret/key sentinels are absent from repr, serialization, argv, logs, exceptions, output, fingerprints, provenance, children, and persisted envelopes beyond the existing public signature.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Hosted signing/restart/tmpfs canaries pass with the required redacted evidence recorded.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py","reason":"Exactly-one startup key source and non-secret service policy."},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py","reason":"Validate/copy one process-owned 0700/0600 key and build the signer runtime."},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/ssm.py","reason":"Remove application runtime SSM retrieval after deployment expansion."},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","reason":"Compose/validate before accepting service work and clean up only the runtime copy."},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py","reason":"Thread context-local signer/principal/push policy through jobs."},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py","reason":"Consume context policy and preserve no-workspace-push."},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"Accept an explicit signer key handle + principal (ensure_opcert_key/opcert_principal/mint_opcert_record/sign_opcert_manifest) instead of reading REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH/REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID from os.environ; env resolution kept as the default for the developer-local close path."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"Thread the context-local signer/principal into sign_completion_verdict; the non-service close-gate caller retains existing env/genesis default behavior via optional params."},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"Thread the optional context-local signer binding through the public sign_manifest (:587) AND its private delegate _sign_manifest_under_lock (:528, the mint_opcert_record caller at :567)."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py","reason":"Thread the optional context-local signer binding through generation.sign_manifest (:261, the plan-review producer calling _sign_manifest_under_lock at :334) so opcert plan-review jobs sign from the injected key, not os.environ."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"Forward the service's context-local signer binding into generation.sign_manifest (:202) on the plan-review signing path; developer-local review-plan passes no binding (env/genesis default)."},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"Inject/mount startup material and remove application key SSM/region inputs."},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert","reason":"Remove application boto3 runtime need and retain process runtime directory contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","reason":"Materialize deployment-owned startup source before service start if SSM remains selected."},{"path":"tests/unit/opcert_service/","reason":"Startup, permissions, restart, context isolation, cleanup, signature, no-SSM, and signer-seam threading oracles."},{"path":"tests/external/test_opcert_startup_live.py","reason":"Hosted signing/restart/tmpfs canary."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11"],["parent","e215-ab23-ed6a-4791"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791","parent_status_uuid":"6ad4950e-32ff-427d-a29c-5f8c2dbaffd2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rp04","opcert","security","auth"],"ticket_id":"6f14-21a7-d806-44b2","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-04 S6 — Move op-cert signing material to startup bindings","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/opcert_service","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Op-cert startup source, permissions, stability, context isolation, cleanup, and no-SSM contract"},{"command":"infra/terraform/opcert-plan-assertions.sh","dd_id":"AC4","dd_text":"Deployment retains pre-start materialization while application loses runtime SSM"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q -m external tests/external/test_opcert_startup_live.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Hosted signing, restart, and tmpfs canary"}]},"source_event_uuids":["a0877319-0b4e-4f69-9dec-c9bb6a724685","69b22c54-02b8-45e0-bad7-1099a89763d2","f31e9f35-c8b9-4594-8d87-f0557a465605","cf525555-7516-4f32-9417-4a656df2f630","3585d8ef-5d94-4e2c-a27b-93e100e67f97","d074cc25-a1a3-4d22-9b3f-171a7618b76a","9980de84-9384-4f86-aba0-ded4a10de49f","1a26d2c1-e6dc-41e5-915d-36678dd4f38c","a8aa831a-64b2-4a98-8c98-e6e911730e28","f0cfa7e5-a583-4e19-86fc-d54bddbcdf25","6e45df50-1f82-4ec6-be7c-e32eecb3b7db","96f1d047-cac5-41ad-a9e4-46ce56f7a629","caea0336-e248-4d51-961e-0bfd673407fd","69930104-3115-4553-932a-9e1587c5c714","24d352fd-1d94-479e-b6c9-4c1385207587","6ad4950e-32ff-427d-a29c-5f8c2dbaffd2","49781188-8b83-4d3f-9649-33d7f29b4143"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787033229301875357,"uuid":"eac18fec-8d91-480f-b4b8-2693a8c57d78"}